\caption(Product-limit survival curves for each group, with right-censoring marked on the curves.)
\alttext(Product-limit survival curves for each group, with right-censoring marked on the curves.)

> Interpretation

A downward step records an event. A censoring removes a subject from later
risk sets and leaves the current survival estimate unchanged. The Prentice
weights change with the pooled event and risk counts, giving earlier
discrepancies more weight than a constant-weight score. The reported normal
reference assumes exchangeable follow-up records under the null.

> References

- [Kaplan and Meier, Nonparametric Estimation from Incomplete Observations|https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1958.10501452]
- [coin survival-score reference|https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/coin/refman/coin.html]
